kground:#8b93b8"></span><b>Grief &amp; Loss</b></td><td class="mono">GRIEF</td><td class="mono dim">duka</td><td class="num"><span class="dash">0</span></td></tr><tr><td><span class="sw" style="background:#ffa94d"></span><b>Morning &amp; Evening</b></td><td class="mono">ADHKAR</td><td class="mono dim">pagi</td><td class="num"><span class="dash">0</span></td></tr><tr><td><span class="sw" style="background:#b8e986"></span><b>Gratitude &amp; Praise</b></td><td class="mono">SHUKR</td><td class="mono dim">syukur</td><td class="num"><span class="dash">0</span></td></tr></tbody></table>
<h3>Kinds</h3>
<table class="t"><thead><tr><th>Kind</th><th>Key</th><th>What it carries</th><th>Cards</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><span class="sw" style="background:#7FA6FF"></span><b>Dua</b></td><td class="mono dim">dua</td><td class="desc">A supplication you say, taken from the Qur&rsquo;an or the sunnah.</td><td class="num">30</td></tr><tr><td><span class="sw" style="background:#E0B341"></span><b>Surah</b></td><td class="mono dim">surah</td><td class="desc">A passage of the Qur&rsquo;an read as recitation. Carries the surah number, its ayah count and its place of revelation in place of a set position.</td><td class="num">5</td></tr></tbody></table>
<div class="note"><b>One category is defined but unused</b>
<p>Food &amp; Drink is one of six categories with a glyph, a colour and a stamp ready but no card in the current 35. Those six stay visible but dimmed in the filter panel, so the deck states what it is going to hold rather than hiding it.</p></div>
</section>

<section id="anatomy"><div class="sh"><span class="no">03</span><h2>Card anatomy</h2></div>
<p class="lede">The card is built on the Methodas card system: a faceted tarot cut at 7:12, one fused panel with
hairline divisions. The front is the reading. The back is the illumination.</p>
