<section id="integrity"><div class="sh"><span class="no">07</span><h2>Content integrity</h2></div>
<p class="lede">These are the rules that decide whether a card is allowed to exist. They outrank design and schedule.</p>
<div class="grid2"><div class="rule"><b>Never author scripture</b><p>Arabic text, hadith and references are transcribed from approved sources. The app may recommend an approved dua; it may never generate one.</p></div><div class="rule"><b>Nothing on a surah card is written by us</b><p>Arabic, translation and transliteration for Surah Set 1 are pulled per chapter from published sources: Tanzil Uthmani (Hafs), Saheeh International, and the transliteration from the same API, each checked against the chapter&rsquo;s own ayah count. Only the use note, the context paragraph and the art brief are ours, and the hadith they reference need a named reviewer before launch like every other claim.</p></div><div class="rule"><b>Canonical text, verified excerpt</b><p>Every Arabic string is the canonical Tanzil Uthmani (Hafs) text, pulled per verse key. Because the cards quote excerpts of longer ayat, each excerpt was located <i>inside</i> its full ayah under Unicode normalisation and the exact canonical characters lifted out, rather than the ayah being pasted over the card. All 30 matched; 4 gained orthographic corrections. Normalise before comparing: آ and ا + madda are the same letter stored two ways, and skipping that step makes 14 correct cards look wrong.</p></div><div class="rule"><b>Every claim carries its source</b><p>Surah and ayah travel with the card, including on copy and share. A card without a checkable source does not ship.</p></div><div class="rule"><b>No guaranteed outcomes</b><p>No dua is presented as securing marriage, wealth, healing, pregnancy or power over another person. Language stays functional.</p></div><div class="rule"><b>Correct, do not copy</b><p>The source design sheets carried mis-attributions. Two were corrected on transcription: Rabbana la tuzigh is Ali ‘Imran 3:8, not Yusuf 99. Rabbana la taj‘alna fitnatan is Al-Mumtahanah 60:5, not Al-Mu’minun 97-98. Flag any further mismatch rather than reproducing it.</p></div><div class="rule"><b>Scholar review before release</b><p>Every card needs a named reviewer and a review date before public launch. The plan carries a Scholar Review Status field for this.</p></div><div class="rule"><b>Premium never gates a dua</b><p>Paying unlocks learning, personalisation, journeys, audio and storage. The religious content is free forever, and the copy says so plainly.</p></div></div>
</section>

